        "description2": "A valve body is the pressure-retaining boundary of a piping system \u2014 its mechanical integrity directly determines the safety and reliability of the entire process line. Forged valve bodies have no internal porosity, no shrinkage cavities, and no residual casting stresses that lead to premature cracking or leakage. The closed-die forging process produces dense, directional grain flow aligned with the hoop stress direction in the body wall, giving forged valve bodies consistently higher pressure ratings, better cyclic load endurance, and more predictable NDT results compared to cast valve bodies. JK Forge produces valve body forgings in ASTM A105, F304, F316, F11, F22, and custom alloys for Class 150 through Class 2500 applications.",
