                "question": "What materials are used for landing gear strut piston and cylinder forgings?",
                "answer": "High-strength low-alloy steels and titanium alloys are the primary material families, selected based on the target aircraft's landing weight class and the strength-to-weight versus fracture toughness tradeoff the specific application calls for. Provide your material specification and load case and our engineering team will confirm forging feasibility."
