        "faqs": [
            {
                "question": "What is a clevis forging and why is forging better than casting for clevis components?",
                "answer": "A clevis is a U-shaped connecting bracket with pin holes used to link two components, especially in towing, lifting, and mechanical linkage applications. Forged clevis components have continuous grain flow through the ear section around the pin bore \u2014 the highest stress point in the assembly. Cast clevis components have random grain structure and can contain microporosity at this critical section, leading to brittle fracture under dynamic loads. Forging consistently delivers 30\u201350% higher fatigue life in clevis ear sections versus equivalent castings."
            },
            {
                "question": "What is the price of forged clevis fittings in India?",
                "answer": "Clevis forging prices depend on material grade (EN8, EN24, stainless), pin size (M12\u2013M80), quantity, WLL certification requirements, and surface finish (plain, galvanized, zinc-plated). JK Forge offers competitive pricing from Rajkot. Email your drawing or specification to sales@JK Forge.com for a quotation within 24 hours. Call +91 92657 72827 for immediate assistance."
            },
            {
                "question": "Which materials do you use for clevis forgings?",
                "answer": "We forge clevis components in EN8 (080M40) for general towing and agricultural applications, EN24 (817M40) for high-tensile lifting and offshore applications, SAE 4140 (42CrMo4) for heavy industrial and mining clevis, SS 304 and SS 316 for corrosion-resistant marine and chemical applications, and IS 2062 for cost-effective structural clevis brackets."
            },
            {
                "question": "Can you provide WLL-rated clevis forgings with test certificates?",
                "answer": "Yes. We produce WLL-rated clevis and rigging hardware with proof-load testing at 2x WLL, magnetic particle inspection, and dimensional verification. Material test certificates (EN 10204 2.2 or 3.1) and proof-load test certificates are issued with each lot. For offshore and marine applications, 3.2 certification through third-party inspection bodies is available."
            },
            {
                "question": "What size clevis forgings can JK Forge produce?",
                "answer": "We produce clevis forgings from M12 pin size (small agricultural clevis pins) up to M80 pin diameter heavy lifting assemblies. Component weights range from 0.1 kg for small jaw ends to 50 kg for heavy tow clevis and drawbar fittings. Custom sizes outside standard ranges are produced to customer drawings."
            },
            {
                "question": "Do you supply D-shackles and rigging hardware as forged components?",
                "answer": "Yes. Bow shackles, D-shackles, connecting links, swivel links, eye bolts, grab hooks, and complete rigging hardware sets are produced at our Rajkot forging facility. We supply to rigging equipment distributors, scaffolding companies, lifting gear suppliers, and direct to construction and port equipment operators."
            },
            {
                "question": "Can you reverse-engineer a clevis from a physical sample?",
                "answer": "Yes. Send us the physical clevis sample or clear dimensional photographs. Our engineering team will take measurements, develop a 2D drawing, design the forging die, and produce a forged prototype for your approval. This service is popular with customers replacing failed cast clevis components with superior forged versions."
            },
            {
                "question": "How do I order clevis forgings from JK Forge in Rajkot?",
                "answer": "Email your drawing (PDF, DXF, STEP), material grade, required WLL or tensile specification, quantity, and any certification requirements to sales@JK Forge.com. We confirm receipt within the same business day and provide a full quotation within 24 hours. You can also call +91 92657 72827 to discuss your requirements directly."
            }
        ]
