                "question": "What is the difference between notched and smooth edge harrow discs?",
                "answer": "Notched edge discs provide more aggressive cutting action, better suited to crop residue incorporation and harder or residue-heavy soil conditions. Smooth edge discs provide cleaner cutting action better suited to finer seedbed preparation where notched-edge aggressiveness isn't required \u2014 selection depends on your specific field conditions and tillage objective."
