                "question": "What is the difference between marine propeller shafts and automotive propeller shafts?",
                "answer": "Marine propeller shafts operate continuously submerged in corrosive seawater, requiring specialized corrosion-resistant alloys like Aquamet or 431 stainless steel. Automotive propeller (drive) shafts operate in a dry, non-corrosive environment and use standard alloy steel grades like EN24 or SAE 4340, with fatigue resistance rather than corrosion resistance as the primary material selection driver."
