                "question": "Why does section thickness matter for heat treatment on components this large?",
                "answer": "Large dipper teeth have substantial mass and section thickness compared to excavator-scale GET, which means heat treatment must be specifically controlled to develop consistent hardness and toughness through that thickness rather than leaving an under-hardened soft core beneath a hardened surface \u2014 a risk that becomes more significant as component mass increases."
