                "question": "What material do you forge valve spring retainers from?",
                "answer": "Alloy steel grades selected specifically for high-cycle fatigue strength at the collet groove, heat treated to the hardness and toughness balance the application's cycle rate and spring load demand. Specific grade recommendation depends on your RPM range and spring specification."
